from pathlib import Path
import json, hashlib, copy
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
PLAN=HERE.parents[1]/'implementation-plan.md'
base=(HERE/'base-plan.md').read_text()
text=base
patches=[]
def patch(feedback,old,new):
 global text
 assert text.count(old)==1,(feedback,old[:100],text.count(old))
 text=text.replace(old,new)
 patches.append({'feedback_id':feedback,'old':old,'new':new})
patch('F07','The current task creates documentation only.','The current task revises this plan and its verification/ledger artifacts and prepares detailed implementation instructions only. The latest user instruction stops this task before code changes. The first future execution milestone is synthetic causal diagnostics and its direct dependencies, ending at the checkpoint below for review.')
patch('F07','Supporting files in `verification/` record the initial scope scaffold, the execution requirement ledger, the feedback delta, and verification evidence.','Supporting files in `verification/` record the initial scope scaffold, the execution requirement ledger, the feedback delta, and verification evidence. The bounded refinement base, current target ledger, exact delta and checks are in `verification/refinement-2026-09-07/`; earlier verification artifacts remain historical and unchanged.')
patch('F01','Freeze the assessment posterior, epsilon, evidence, inventory, denominator and selected set before evaluating Bank B. B must never affect selection, stopping, posterior updates, the reported production result or subsequent answers.','Freeze the assessment posterior, epsilon, evidence, inventory, denominator and selected set before evaluating B1 or B2. Neither evaluation bank may affect selection, stopping, posterior updates, the reported production result or subsequent answers. References to B below mean the separately identified B1 and B2 families; never pool them into a single unexplained estimate.\n\n- **B1:** use the same deterministic theta strata/posterior positions as production A, with independent latent-item draws. Preserve the production theta-stratum weights; if a larger bank repeats these positions, freeze and report the replication/weighting scheme. This isolates Bernoulli/latent-item mask-bank effects while holding the theta approximation fixed.\n- **B2:** use independently randomized or shifted stratified posterior positions, plus independent latent-item draws. Freeze the position-generation method and seed derivation before outcomes. This probes the broader finite predictive approximation, including theta-position effects. B2 must not merely reuse A\'s deterministic theta positions or B1\'s masks.\n\nProduction A remains unchanged in both comparisons. Retain separate fingerprints for theta positions and latent-item draw streams for A, B1 and B2. Independence describes the randomized dimensions: B1 deliberately shares A\'s deterministic theta strata.')
patch('F01','Parameterize independent seed material and evaluation sample count only for the explicit diagnostic call.','Parameterize independent seed material, evaluation sample count and the explicit B1/B2 sampling mode only for the diagnostic call.')
patch('F01','A seed change must affect all stochastic dimensions present in the sampler; deterministic theta stratification must be described honestly rather than claiming every bank component is randomized. Repeated copies of A or its masks are not independent banks.','A latent-item seed change must affect that draw stream without changing B1 theta positions; a B2 position seed change must affect its randomized/shifted posterior positions independently of latent-item seeds. Deterministic B1 theta stratification must be described honestly rather than claiming every bank component is randomized. Repeated copies of A or its masks are not independent banks.')
patch('F01','For fixed D report Q0.05(A), Q0.05(B) for each replicate, their difference, estimated probability of coverage below 0.98 under B, and numerical variability.','For fixed D report Q0.05(A), Q0.05(B1) and Q0.05(B2) for each replicate, their differences, estimated probability of coverage below 0.98 under each evaluation family, and numerical variability. Compare A/B1 for latent-item bank effects and B1/B2 for sensitivity to the broader theta-position approximation, retaining the uncertainty of each comparison; neither contrast alone proves a causal mechanism.')
patch('F01','same diagnostic manifest produces identical artifacts; B changes when its seed changes;','same diagnostic manifest produces identical artifacts; seed changes affect only the intended B1/B2 dimensions; fixed-bank fixtures verify exact A/B1 theta-position identity and B2 position independence;')
patch('F01','predictive A, evaluation B, and diagnostic success sampling separate.','predictive A, B1 latent-item draws, B2 posterior positions, B2 latent-item draws, and diagnostic success sampling separate.')
patch('F02','Choose the development reader/document counts from a precision/runtime plan','Maintain three distinct synthetic data roles in that order: freely reusable diagnostic-development data; a fresh **development-confirmation** seed/document set; and the unchanged frozen release holdout. Reserve the development-confirmation manifest separately, with seed/document identities or immutable generation provenance and non-overlap checks. Do not use or inspect its outcomes during iterative design. Freeze the diagnostic/model candidate, configuration, analysis and decision rules before its first development-confirmation evaluation, and record that freeze with source/artifact hashes. Use this intermediate set before any release-holdout access. If its results motivate design changes, return to diagnostic-development data, retain the failed/null result and treat that set as consumed for that candidate-design cycle; a subsequent frozen candidate needs a fresh development-confirmation set. This adds a supplementary confirmation stage without changing release gates, holdout contents or the version-2 golden. Reserving manifests is allowed in the first milestone; accessing development-confirmation outcomes or the release holdout is outside that milestone.\n\nChoose the development reader/document counts from a precision/runtime plan')
patch('F06','The small-document census can supply direct selected-card labels, but a census remains subject to criterion ambiguity and participant effects.','The small-document census can supply direct selected-card labels, but a census remains subject to criterion ambiguity and participant effects.\n\nDesign rehearsals must report minimum inclusion probability, maximum design weight, effective sample size, and expected selected-card/final-tail support, with the frame, weighting convention, effective-sample-size definition and relevant participant/document/item grouping explicit. Examine sparse or empty selected-card/tail cells and sensitivity to unequal weights; do not confuse a weight-based effective sample size with independent participant/document support. These diagnostics inform the eventual SAP/design freeze. This plan supplies no numerical thresholds, trimming rules or estimator defaults for them.')
patch('F03','The amendment removes sampling circularity; it does not prove noninterference.','The amendment removes sampling circularity; it does not prove noninterference. **Pretest interference is an explicit blocking decision for confirmatory human collection:** confirmation must not proceed until evidence supports the chosen pretest procedure or the reviewed study design explicitly accounts for interference. Record the supporting evidence or design treatment, responsible review and freeze decision before confirmatory collection. Developmental studies may measure interference without satisfying this confirmation gate.')
patch('F04','Freeze the target-sense mapping before observing answers or model outcomes where feasible.','For confirmatory criterion scoring, the target-sense/context mapping and scoring rubric must be frozen before confirmatory responses or model outcomes are inspected. There is no feasibility exception. Developmental rubric refinement must remain outside the confirmatory scoring material; ambiguities discovered later follow the frozen ambiguity/adjudication procedure and recorded amendment rules, rather than outcome-informed rewriting.')
patch('F06','Negative controls deliberately introduce post-reveal criteria, invalid/changed weights,','Sampling-design rehearsal outputs include the minimum inclusion probability, maximum design weight, effective sample size and expected selected-card/final-tail support specified above, alongside realized support. Sparse support and extreme weights must remain visible as design findings for the SAP; this rehearsal does not choose numerical acceptance thresholds.\n\nNegative controls deliberately introduce post-reveal criteria, invalid/changed weights,')
patch('F03','Confirmation remains blocked until primary endpoint gaps are resolved under the approved SAP;','Confirmation remains blocked until primary endpoint gaps and the pretest-interference decision are resolved under the approved SAP/design;')
patch('F06','Independent learners per item, not total rows, govern empirical item calibration eligibility.','Include minimum inclusion probability, maximum design weight, effective sample size and expected selected-card/final-tail support from design rehearsals; statistical review must define their interpretation and any resulting design limits before the SAP/design freeze, without adopting numerical thresholds from this plan. Independent learners per item, not total rows, govern empirical item calibration eligibility.')
patch('F03','Any post-freeze amendment retains its rationale, authorization and original analysis; no outcome-driven estimator choice.','The freeze must explicitly close the pretest-interference blocking decision through supporting evidence or a design that accounts for interference. Any post-freeze amendment retains its rationale, authorization and original analysis; no outcome-driven estimator choice.')
patch('F05','Prioritize the simple baselines already named in the pilot:','Separate the **core human validity study** from the **broader equal-total-preparation-time product-value comparison**. Core validity establishes item calibration, deck validity, realized coverage, burden and warm non-inferiority under its approved design. The broader product-value comparison remains valuable planned work, but does not automatically block those core claims or their study completion unless a specifically identified authoritative requirement makes it a release prerequisite. Trace any such prerequisite to its canonical requirement ID before applying it; this companion neither invents a new release gate nor removes an existing one. Verified learning and delayed retention needed by a core endpoint remain required by that endpoint, even if the broader comparison is scheduled separately.\n\nFor the broader comparison, prioritize the simple baselines already named in the pilot:')
patch('F03','| Human theta interval |','| Pretest interference | Evidence supporting the chosen pretest procedure or a reviewed design explicitly accounting for interference | Blocking decision before confirmatory human collection; developmental measurement is allowed |\n| Human theta interval |')
patch('F04','| Meaning prompt/ambiguity | Multiple context-free meanings, hidden target context for blinded raters, separate ambiguity status | Freeze protocol/rubric and any consent/schema delta before real use; fabricated scoring examples can proceed |','| Meaning prompt/ambiguity | Multiple context-free meanings, hidden target context for blinded raters, separate ambiguity status | Freeze target-sense/context mapping and scoring rubric before inspecting confirmatory responses or model outcomes, with no feasibility exception; freeze any consent/schema delta before real use; fabricated scoring examples can proceed |')
patch('F06','| Estimation and precision | Named estimator/variance/missingness/multiplicity/design with justified participant/document support |','| Estimation and precision | Named estimator/variance/missingness/multiplicity/design with justified participant/document support, minimum inclusion probability, maximum weight, effective sample size and expected selected-card/final-tail support; no numerical thresholds supplied here |')
patch('F01','| Diagnostic run design | Development seeds, B sample sizes/replicates, budgets, coupling and materiality/precision rules |','| Diagnostic run design | Development seeds, distinct B1/B2 modes and sample sizes/replicates, budgets, coupling and materiality/precision rules |')
patch('F02','| POS and usability decisions |','| Synthetic data access | Diagnostic-development, untouched development-confirmation, then frozen release holdout | Freeze candidate/analysis/decision rules before development-confirmation access; no iterative use; confirmation precedes release holdout; retain and retire consumed confirmation sets after design changes |\n| POS and usability decisions |')
patch('F05','Prepare reviewable deltas against the accepted files,','Core validity and the broader equal-time value comparison have separate completion decisions; only an identified authoritative release prerequisite can make the latter block core validity.\n\nPrepare reviewable deltas against the accepted files,')
patch('F07','No permission question is required to finish the present planning task.','The latest user instruction limits the present task to plan revision and implementation handoff instructions, stopping before code changes. The future first synthetic causal-diagnostics milestone must stop at its review checkpoint before beginning subsequent slices.')
patch('F01','Reproducible A/B diagnostic report with uncertainty and no runtime behavior change','Reproducible A/B1/B2 diagnostic report with uncertainty and no runtime behavior change')
patch('F05','| SAP/design |','| Broader product-value comparison | Study owner: equal-total-preparation-time baselines and ordinary-use comparison | Separate design/SAP; not an automatic prerequisite for core human validity absent a cited authoritative requirement | Independently interpretable value/burden report; no inferred new release gate |\n| SAP/design |')
patch('F07','Each slice is independently reviewable and testable.','**First future execution boundary (not code authorization for this documentation task):** implement Foundation and Forensic banks as the first synthetic causal-diagnostics milestone, including natural/fixed-budget/common-replay counterfactual infrastructure only where it is a direct dependency. The milestone includes failed-deck records, exact occurrence-mass conservation, immutable A/B1/B2 frozen-deck evaluation, reproducibility/RNG-stream controls, fixed-bank and small-enumeration oracle fixtures. Do not implement study-data schema changes, production selector changes, warm-production changes, POS policy changes, calibration slots, or release-holdout tuning. Subsequent slices remain planned work, not authorization to execute them during this milestone.\n\nAt its checkpoint, stop for review and report changed files; mathematical/statistical invariants; proof that production outputs are unchanged with diagnostics off; deterministic/reproducibility tests; narrow test results; diagnostic overhead; discovered design issues; and a reasoned recommendation on proceeding to the longitudinal-warm slice. A recommendation is not permission to begin that slice.\n\nEach slice is independently reviewable and testable.')
patch('F02','3. Run the complete evaluator and the frozen release holdout only after candidate freeze, preserving its original seed/population/gate definitions.','3. Evaluate the frozen candidate first on the fresh, previously untouched development-confirmation seed/document set under its frozen analysis/decision rules. Do not inspect that set during iterative design. If it motivates changes, retain the result, return to diagnostic-development work and reserve a fresh confirmation set for the next frozen candidate. Run the complete evaluator and the frozen release holdout only after candidate freeze and the separate development-confirmation decision permits progression, preserving its original seed/population/gate definitions.')
patch('F03','under the frozen protocol/SAP before making its gated claims.','under the frozen protocol/SAP, with the pretest-interference blocking decision resolved and target-sense/context mapping plus rubric frozen before confirmatory outcome inspection, before making its gated claims.')
